-- LINEARITY ---- errors/linear_mixed_consumption_5.march

The linear value `state.sessions` is used more than once here. [linear_used_twice]
Linear values must be consumed exactly once — they cannot be copied or ignored.

15 |         Some(s) -> { state with done: state.done + sink(s) }
                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    `{ state with … }` keeps every field it doesn't replace, so the old `state.sessions` would survive into the new record. Replace it too: `{ state with sessions: … }`.

    `state.sessions` was already consumed here:

12 |       let (got, m) = LinearMap.take(state.sessions, sid)
                                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    run `march --explain linear_used_twice`


